# File & Folder Organization

## Flat structure

- Prefer flat folders over deep nesting
- Route folders (`app/[route]/`): keep `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx` and co-located modules in the same folder

## Prefix-based grouping

- Use consistent prefixes for related files: `demo.tsx`, `demo-placeholder.tsx`, `demo-buttons.tsx`
- File Nesting (configured globally in Cursor/VS Code) groups `demo-*.tsx` under `demo.tsx` in the explorer

## When to use subfolders

- Only when there are many related files (>5) or distinct domains (e.g. features, api routes)
- Avoid creating `components/`, `data/`, `utils/` subfolders for a single route unless justified
